  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) is our best at 0.5856 acc, and config_041 (same but scgpt) at 0.5200 confirms pca_n2000 is the stronger RNA encoder. config_025 (image_only) at 0.2596 confirms multimodal is essential. Uncertainty: We have only tested 'weighted' fusion in the top-performing setup; the alternative 'concat' fusion is untested with this exact configuration. This experiment (config_039) changes only the fusion from weighted to concat while holding all other hyperparameters at their best-known values (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, transformer). This is a clean single-variable ablation that clarifies whether the weighted combination is genuinely superior or whether a simpler concatenation could match or exceed it. With 6 experiments remaining, confirming or rejecting the fusion choice early reduces the search space and guides subsequent experiments toward the most promising architecture."
